    "body": "Fixes #7008.\n\nA fused type in a special method (e.g. `__cinit__`, `__getitem__`) currently makes the fused dispatcher emit a `PyMethodDef` initialised with a function definition. Cython exits 0 and the C compiler then fails with `expected expression before 'static'`. Raise a `CompileError` at the definition instead, so the failure points at the source line.\n\nThis does not add support for fused special methods; it turns invalid C into a clear error. The same dispatch path is broken for `__getitem__` (#6872).\n\nTests on B300 x86 (GCC 13.3, Python 3.12):\n- new `tests/errors/e_fused_special_method.pyx` passes.\n- `fused_cpdef`, `fused_def`, `fused_cdef`, `check_fused_types` all pass.\n\nAI assistance was used for the investigation, implementation, and test drafting.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
